CLUBS` with 25 `4 runners`, 50 `3 runners`, 100 `1 runner`,\n40\t    and a grey 25 `2 volunteers`;\n41\t  - the footer.\n42\t\n43\t  The stress renders all read correctly:\n44\t  - `extra/long-1920x1080.png` shows `1,204` and `#1043`;\n45\t  - `extra/maxed-1080x1080.png` shows `9,999` with no clipping;\n46\t  - in `extra/ten-1080x1920.png`, ten clubs make 5 + 5 with the right\n47\t    singular and plural (`1 runner`, `1 volunteer`);\n48\t  - `extra/empty-1080x1080.png` keeps the band and shows `No milestone clubs\n49\t    this week`.\n50\t\n51\t  The auditor found every refusal the brief lists, each naming the field and\n52\t  value. On top of those it refuses negatives, 3.5, 10000, `0xR25`, a bare\n53\t  `R25` and misspelled props. The weekday uses Sakamoto's method; 1900-02-29\n54\t  is refused and 2000-02-29 is accepted. No test is empty.\n55\t- **Wrong, layout (line 4).**\n56\t  - On the default square (`stills/square.png`) the four stat tiles sit 3-7\n57\t    px inside the hero and band edges. The right edge is at x=1030 against\n58\t    1037. The gaps between them are 28-32 px, against 25 between the hero\n59\t    tiles. This is the lattice snap, and the build admits it.\n60\t  - Six clubs at 1920x1080 (`extra/long-1920x1080.png`) are drawn as 144x81\n61\t    badges in two rows: 134 px apart side to side, 22 px top to bottom, in a\n62\t    band that is mostly empty. The `MILESTONE CLUBS` title (about 37 px) is\n63\t    bigger than the club numbers. One row of six would fit at about 200 px\n64\t    wide.\n65\t  - In `stills/landscape.png` the hero labels sit lower than the stat labels\n66\t    in the same row: `finishers` at y≈404, `new PBs` at y≈380.\n67\t- **Wrong, smaller.**\n68\t  - The accent's 4.5:1 check is made against the tile `#fbfbfb`, not the page\n69\t    as the brief says (L320).\n70\t  - `milestones \",,,\"` silently gives the empty week, and `4xR025` and\n71\t    `001xR25` are read without complaint.\n72\t  - The contract cannot say \"exactly 2 hero / 4 stat tiles\", and tile labels\n73\t    have no presence entry of their own. The test covers the count only\n74\t    through text sizes.\n75\t  - `stills/tutorial-6.png` reads \"3 phases - 22m 54s - $18\": scout, plan and\n76\t    plan (2). It leaves out build call 1 (95 min, $28.58, timed out), which had\n77\t    already run when this tutorial was rendered at 20:49Z. Day 016's page also\n78\t    stops before build, so this is the tutorial tool's doing, not a's code.\n79\t    Still, the page undercounts the day.\n80\t\n81\t**b: six equal tiles**\n82\t\n83\t- **Right.** `stills/square.png` is a tidy 3x2 board in the runstats order,\n84\t  with one number size and every string right. `stills/tutorial-3.png`\n85\t  describes six equal tiles honestly.\n86\t- **Wrong, design.** The hierarchy is gone. In `stills/landscape.png` and the\n87\t  square, `31 volunteers` sits mid-grid in row two at the same size as\n88\t  `19 visitors`. Brief rubric 1 (\"214 ran, 31 volunteered\" in two seconds,\n89\t  headline at least 1.5x the stats) fails by construction.\n90\t- **Wrong, code.** b was built before the review fixes:\n91\t  - It has no unknown-prop refusal (no \"did you mean\" in its source), so\n92\t    `count` for `counts` prints the sample week under a real event name.\n93\t  - Club counts are not checked against finishers or volunteers.\n94\t  - Six clubs draw one row on wide canvases, against the brief's 5-per-row.\n95\t  - Six to ten clubs are refused on 1000x800, 1200x900, 1290x1000 and\n96\t    1440x900.\n97\t  - A `counts` JSON string is not parsed.\n98\t  - The footer has a 70-character cap the brief never set.\n99\t\n100\t**c: a on a night page**\n101\t\n102\t- **Right.** `stills/square.png` reads well. The light-green badges carry dark\n103\t  text, the grey volunteer badge white text, and the accent `#3fae74` keeps\n104\t  the hero numbers legible.\n105\t- **Wrong, design.** Tiles are only 1.19:1 against the `#14211a` page, so the\n106\t  tile edges nearly